metadata:
  project: E36 Restomod -- CWA400 Electric Water Pump Wiring (PHASE 3)
  phase: "Phase 3 (07K swap moment — electric water pump replaces belt-driven OEM pump; PMU16 arrives concurrently)"
  description: >-
    ⚠️ PHASE 3 INSTALL FILE. The CWA400 electric water pump is installed at the
    07K engine swap — the belt-driven OEM water pump is removed with the M52.
    Under Phase 1 (M52 in car) the OEM belt-driven pump is still spinning and
    NO electric pump wiring exists. PMU16 also arrives at Phase 3 (see
    harnesses/power-distribution.wv), so all EWP wiring is Phase 3 install.

    Pierburg CWA400 (PWM version) powered by Ecumaster PMU16 O5+O14 parallel
    outputs (50A combined) and controlled by MaxxECU RACE H2O via PWM GPO.
    OEM pump 07K121011B impeller removed, housing stays as coolant manifold.
    No separate pump controller -- MaxxECU is the sole PWM driver.
    PMU16 O5+O14 wire direct to CWA400 Pin 3. Post-shutdown cooling managed
    by PMU16 (no separate power-hold relay needed).

    Under the H2O engine-bay-mount architecture: MaxxECU RACE H2O, PMU16, and CWA400
    are ALL engine-bay-mounted (see docs/vendor/maxxecu/MaxxECU_RACE_H2O.md §8 and
    harnesses/power-distribution.wv). CWA400 wiring is entirely engine-bay-to-
    engine-bay — no firewall crossing.

    Cross-reference ewp-wiring-reference.md for full specs, part numbers,
    duty cycle map, and post-shutdown config.
    Confirmed: @wingman703 (07K/8HP build, identical drivetrain).

# ── TODO list ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   [ ] Verify CWA400 part number on sourced unit -- PWM version only
#       (Pierburg 7.07223.10.0 / BMW 11515A05704 / 11517563659 / 11517568594)
#       Do NOT accept Pierburg 7.03665.66.0 or BMW 11517604027 (LIN version)
#   [ ] Confirm PMU16 O14 physical pin number -- see PMU-16_Pinout_v1.2.pdf
#       (ecumaster.com/files/PMU/PMU-16_Pinout_v1.2.pdf)
#   [ ] Configure PMU software: set O5 + O14 as parallel output pair
#   [ ] Program post-shutdown EWP logic in PMU software:
#       keep O5+O14 active after key-off until MaxxECU CAN CLT < 70C
#       OR 3-min fallback timer -- whichever comes first
#   [ ] Confirm MaxxECU RACE GPO pin assignment for CWA400 PWM signal
#   [ ] Set MaxxECU PWM output frequency to 680 Hz in software
#   [ ] Verify wake pulse config: MaxxECU must send >= 3ms high pulse at
#       ignition-on before transitioning to CLT duty-cycle map
#   [ ] Bleeding procedure: tie Pin 1 to +12V (forces emergency run) +
#       Pin 3 direct to BATT+ before PMU16 connection for pre-fire bleed/leak test
#   [ ] Confirm Kostal 2+2 connector and terminals sourced before Phase 3 build

# ── Connectors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

connectors:

  PMU16_EWP_STUB:
    type: "Stub: PMU16 O5+O14 parallel → CWA400 Pin 3"
    subtype: "Cross-reference harnesses/power-distribution.wv PMU16 pins 10+13"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels:
      - "O5 +12V (PHYS pin 12 -- 25A)"
      - "O14 +12V (PHYS pin 14 -- 25A)"
    notes: >-
      O5 and O14 wired in parallel -- join at CWA400 Pin 3 terminal.
      Combined 50A rating handles CWA400 35.5A nominal draw.
      8 AWG per wire minimum. Configure as parallel pair in PMU software.
      PMU16 M6 stud is BATT+ always-on -- O5+O14 can activate post key-off
      for cooling soak without a separate BATT+ relay or power-hold relay.
      See power-distribution.wv for upstream wiring (BATT+, ANL fuse, PMU16 stud).

  CHASSIS_GND:
    type: "Chassis ground stud (body metal)"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["GND"]
    notes: >-
      Dedicated ground for pump Pin 4 -- do not share with signal grounds
      or high-current grounds from other loads (fan motor, fuel pump).
      10 AWG minimum. Ring terminal, solid bolt to body metal.

  MAXXECU_GPO:
    type: "MaxxECU RACE -- PWM General Purpose Output"
    subtype: "GPO pin TBD -- confirm in MaxxECU pin assignment"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["PWM signal out (680 Hz)"]
    notes: >-
      MaxxECU GPO configured as PWM output at 680 Hz.
      CLT-to-duty-cycle map: 20% at 60C / 55% at 85C / 97% at 105C.
      MaxxECU GPO high = 12V; CWA400 requires V_Hi at least 0.6 x Ub (~7.2V) -- compliant.
      Wake pulse: MaxxECU must output at least 3ms uninterrupted high at ignition-on
      before transitioning to CLT map -- configure startup duty override in software.
      Duty cycle 0-12%: pump off or emergency run -- do not use in normal map.
      Duty cycle 13-85%: controlled operation (linear min to max speed).
      Duty cycle 86-97%: full speed. 98-100%: emergency run (~5900 RPM).

  CWA400_PUMP:
    type: "Pierburg CWA400 (PWM version) -- Kostal 2+2 connector"
    subtype: "150 LPM @ 0.85 bar -- installed in lower radiator hose"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels:
      - "Pin 1 (PWM signal in -- from MaxxECU GPO)"
      - "Pin 2 (BSD diagnostic -- leave floating)"
      - "Pin 3 (+12V power -- from PMU16 O5+O14 parallel)"
      - "Pin 4 (GND)"
    notes: >-
      PWM version ONLY: Pierburg 7.07223.10.0 / BMW 11515A05704 / 11517563659.
      Do NOT use LIN version (Pierburg 7.03665.66.0 / BMW 11517604027).
      Connector: Kostal 2+2 (10098866). Pins 1-2: SLK 2.8 ELA terminals (22124499560).
      Pins 3-4: SLK 5.8 ELA terminals (22124544900).
      Install inline in lower radiator hose (cold/return side), outlet toward engine.
      Pin 2 (BSD): leave floating -- not used with MaxxECU PWM control.
      35.5A nominal draw -- 8 AWG minimum on Pin 3 (PMU16 O5+O14 parallel feeds here).
      Datasheet: https://tecomotive.com/download/datasheets/CWA400_PWM_EN.pdf
      Product: https://www.tecomotive.com/en/products/CWA400_PWM.html

# ── Cables ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

cables:

  CABLE_PWR_O5:
    gauge: "8 AWG"
    length: "1.5 m"
    colors: [RD]
    wirecount: 1
    notes: >-
      PMU16 O5 to CWA400 Pin 3 (parallel A). 8 AWG minimum.
      Route from PMU16 through engine bay to pump location.
      Join to CABLE_PWR_O14 at Pin 3 terminal (parallel junction).

  CABLE_PWR_O14:
    gauge: "8 AWG"
    length: "1.5 m"
    colors: [RD]
    wirecount: 1
    notes: >-
      PMU16 O14 to CWA400 Pin 3 (parallel B). 8 AWG minimum.
      Route alongside CABLE_PWR_O5 -- keep both runs the same length
      to balance current sharing between the two parallel outputs.
      Join to CABLE_PWR_O5 at Pin 3 terminal (parallel junction).

  CABLE_GND:
    gauge: "10 AWG"
    length: "1.5 m"
    colors: [BK]
    wirecount: 1
    notes: >-
      CWA400 Pin 4 to chassis ground stud.
      10 AWG minimum. Dedicated ground -- do not share.

  CABLE_PWM:
    gauge: "22 AWG"
    length: "2.0 m"
    colors: [VT]
    wirecount: 1
    notes: >-
      MaxxECU GPO to CWA400 Pin 1 (PWM signal).
      22 AWG signal wire. Route from ECU through firewall grommet to pump.
      Keep away from ignition coil wiring and high-current runs where possible.
      Shielded wire preferred for EMC -- drain to chassis GND at ECU end only.

# ── Connections ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

connections:
  # PMU16 O5 → CWA400 Pin 3 (+12V parallel A)
  -
    - PMU16_EWP_STUB: [1]
    - CABLE_PWR_O5: [1]
    - CWA400_PUMP: [3]
  # PMU16 O14 → CWA400 Pin 3 (+12V parallel B)
  -
    - PMU16_EWP_STUB: [2]
    - CABLE_PWR_O14: [1]
    - CWA400_PUMP: [3]
  # Pump Pin 4 → chassis GND
  -
    - CWA400_PUMP: [4]
    - CABLE_GND: [1]
    - CHASSIS_GND: [1]
  # MaxxECU GPO → pump Pin 1 (PWM signal)
  -
    - MAXXECU_GPO: [1]
    - CABLE_PWM: [1]
    - CWA400_PUMP: [1]
